{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1530,
    "dDurationMs": 4739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rainbow, as we know it, is Red, Orange,\nYellow, Green, Blue, Violet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6269,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ROYGBV."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7269,
    "dDurationMs": 2301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm ignoring Indigo because, let's be honest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9570,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indigo?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10570,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But where exactly is violet?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12120,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it at the end here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13370,
    "dDurationMs": 1469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This dark blue?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14839,
    "dDurationMs": 1521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what’s this brighter light blue-green?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16360,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cyan, perhaps?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17530,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why don't we say the rainbow is Red Orange\nYellow Green Cyan Blue?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21800,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ROYGCB"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23270,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we actually do, and we’ve just forgotten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26140,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When Isaac Newton originally observed a rainbow\nof light split by a prism and made his labeling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30460,
    "dDurationMs": 4599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the colors as RedOrangeYellowGreenBlueIndigoViolet,\nthe thing he called “blue” was indeed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35059,
    "dDurationMs": 5291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we would now call blue-green, teal or\ncyan – reminiscent of the color of the blue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40350,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41350,
    "dDurationMs": 4009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what we now tend to call blue, Newton\ncalled violet - as in, roses are red, violets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45359,
    "dDurationMs": 1241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46600,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dark blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47600,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He only included indigo in his fundamental\n\"seven colors of the rainbow” so that they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51300,
    "dDurationMs": 6739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would match the number of notes of the western\nmusical scale: Do re mi fa so la ti… yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58039,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Purple and magenta, as we know, don't occur\nin the rainbow from a prism because they can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62639,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only be made as a combination of red and blue\nlight, and those are on opposite sides of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66700,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rainbow – nowhere near overlapping."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69200,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there’s no purple or hot pink in the\nrainbow from a prism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72950,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Violet is there in the “roses are red, violets\nare BLUE” sense, but purple is not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78380,
    "dDurationMs": 3559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So then why do rainbows in the sky often look\nlike they have purple in them?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81939,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I suspect sometimes it's an optical illusion\nwhereby nice deep blues in small amounts surrounded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86969,
    "dDurationMs": 2981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a lighter color appear purplish to our\neyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89950,
    "dDurationMs": 4529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "HOWEVER, sometimes purple and pink really\nARE there - because a rainbow is really a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94479,
    "dDurationMs": 5471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rain-disk: each color of sunlight reflects\nback in a bright-rimmed disc, all of different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99950,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sizes, which together add up to make a white\ndisk with a colorful rim."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103969,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because light is a wave, interference\nfrom the raindrops themselves actually gives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108090,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each disk multiple rings - the familiar outer\nring is just the brightest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112429,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The others are called \"supernumerary rings\"\nand are the source of supernumerary rainbows"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116700,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- the smaller the raindrops, the stronger\nthe supernumerary bows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120510,
    "dDurationMs": 4609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if the drops are the right size, the first\nred supernumerary ring can overlap significantly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125119,
    "dDurationMs": 3971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the main dark blue ring, and what do\nred and blue give?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129090,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Purple!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130090,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as the saying goes, roses are red, violets\nare blue, and purple in a rainbow is a supernumerary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135510,
    "dDurationMs": 37140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hue."
    } ]
  } ]
}
